==Betawi==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|bew|kitah}} (Bekasi dialect)
* {{alter|bew|kite}} (Tanah Abang dialect)
* {{alter|bew|kitè}} (Meester dialect)

===Etymology===
From {{der|bew|poz-mly-pro|*kita(ʔ)}}, from {{der|bew|poz-pro|*(i-)kita}}, from {{der|bew|map-pro|*(i-)kita}}. Compare {{cog|tl|kita}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|literary}} {{IPA|bew|/kiˈta/}}
* {{a|Bekasi}} {{IPA|bew|/kiˈtah/}}
* {{a|Tanah Abang}} {{IPA|bew|/kiˈtəː/}}
* {{a|Meester}} {{IPA|bew|/kiˈtɛ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q33014 (bew)-Bangrapip-kita.wav|Literary dialect}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q33014 (bew)-Bangrapip-kitè.wav|Meester dialect}}
* {{hyphenation|bew|ki|ta}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|bew|pronoun}}

# [[we]]
#: {{ux|bew|'''Kita''' ni ari bakal pegi ke Bandung.|'''We''' are going to Bandung today.}}
# [[our]] / [[ours]]
#: {{ux|bew|Ada orang ngebètak bola '''kita'''.|Someone seized (stole) '''our''' ball.}}
# {{lb|bew|euphemistic}} [[I]]
#: {{syn|bew|gua}}

====Usage notes====
* Sometimes, instead of {{l|bew|gua}}, someone may use {{l|bew|kita}} for more politeness reason.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|bew|ané}}
* {{l|bew|gua}}

